{"timestamp": "2025-07-29T21:41:58.032685", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "    initial_state = env._current_state\n\n    # Queue stores tuples of (state, list_of_actions_to_reach_this_state)\n    # Using collections.deque for efficient appends and pops from both ends.\n    queue = collections.deque([(initial_state, [])])\n\n    # Visited set to store hashable representations of states\n    # A state is uniquely defined by its grid, inventory, position, and direction.\n    # Convert numpy arrays (grid, inventory) to bytes for hashing.\n    visited = set()\n\n    # Define the possible actions.\n    # env_factory.N_ACTIONS provides the total number of actions (typically 5: 4 directions + USE).\n    ACTIONS = range(env_factory.N_ACTIONS)\n\n    # Helper function to create a hashable key for a state\n    def get_state_key(state):\n        # Convert numpy arrays to bytes objects, which are hashable.\n        return (state.grid.tobytes(), state.inventory.tobytes(), state.pos, state.dir)\n\n    # Add the initial state to the visited set to avoid reprocessing.\n    visited.add(get_state_key(initial_state))\n\n    # Breadth-First Search (BFS) loop\n    while queue:\n        current_state, path = queue.popleft()  # Get the state and its path from the front of the queue\n\n        # Check if the current state satisfies the goal (i.e., the item is in inventory)\n        # goal_name is ignored by CraftState.satisfies, goal_arg is the item index.\n        if current_state.satisfies(None, item):\n            return path  # Goal reached, return the sequence of actions\n\n        # Explore all possible actions from the current state\n        for action in ACTIONS:\n            # Simulate the action to get the next state\n            # CraftState.step returns (reward, new_state). Reward is always 0.0 here.\n            _reward, next_state = current_state.step(action)\n\n            next_state_key = get_state_key(next_state)\n\n            # If this next state has not been visited, add it to the queue and visited set\n            if next_state_key not in visited:\n                visited.add(next_state_key)\n                new_path = path + [action]  # Append the current action to the path\n                queue.append((next_state, new_path)) # Add the new state and its path to the queue\n\n    # If the queue becomes empty and the goal was not reached,\n    # it means the item cannot be crafted or is unreachable within the search space.\n    return []", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": -1}}
